representation:"n:ℕ encodes all nonnegative ambient dimensions, including zero. YEuclid m is EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin m)=PiLp 2 (fun _ : Fin m => ℝ); the 2 is the Lp metric exponent in ℝ≥0∞, not the number of coordinates. Ordinary function/product types have a different metric, so yProd E lives directly in YEuclid (n+1). yHoriz uses Fin.castSucc for the first n coordinates, yVert uses Fin.last n for the last, and yJoin uses Fin.snoc. The proof workers must check yHoriz(yJoin x t)=x, yVert(yJoin x t)=t, yJoin(yHoriz z)(yVert z)=z and the squared-distance formula when used; none is hidden in a definition. yI is the usual scalar [0,1]; this is the canonical scalar presentation of R^1 in the source's one-dimensional specializations. N001 explicitly carries this specialization as well as its coordinate-space family, each proved by the same supplied cover argument, without needing an auxiliary representation transfer. Metric.ediam is the supremum of extended pairwise distances, zero for empty sets. yContent uses ℕ-sequences (finite families padded by empty sets), an indexed infimum over coverage and diameter proofs, and a nonnegative extended tsum. yHaus is the supremum over positive real scales. These are used only at positive exponents, so empty members have zero rpow cost. A missing admissible cover has infimum top. dimH is the pinned native ℝ≥0∞ Hausdorff dimension using its internal Borel structure and the supremum of nonnegative NNReal exponents with infinite native measure; it is not coerced to a real before finiteness is proved. ENNReal.ofReal embeds nonnegative real scales/exponents and truncates negative inputs, so every such use is guarded by positivity. Native critical-exponent APIs take NNReal exponents; use ⟨s,le_of_lt hs⟩. Finite diameters and D may be converted using .toReal only with an explicit not-top fact and ENNReal.ofReal_toReal. yCritical is merely a conjunction defining the exact obligations, not a proved property or premise. All M facts are direct pinned-library uses; Audit A notes remain optional references and add no ports.",
