source_outputs:{N001:"T001",N002:"T002",N003:"T005",N004:"T009",N005:"T011",N006:"T012",N007:"T013",P:"T014"},
endpoint_correspondence:{P:{mode:"direct",explanation:"For arbitrary n:ℕ and E:Set(EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n)), H001 retains 0≤n, H002 retains nonemptiness and H003 retains compactness for the Euclidean metric. The target is the native Hausdorff dimension equality in ℝ≥0∞. Membership in yProd E means that the first n coordinates lie in E and the last lies in the scalar closed interval [0,1]; this is exactly the specified coordinate identification of E×[0,1] with a subset of Euclidean R^(n+1). EuclideanSpace uses the L2 metric, including the unique empty vector at n=0, so both sides, all hypotheses and the full parameter domain are unchanged. No maximum-product norm or extra finiteness assumption occurs."}}
